WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.321
Here is the Shuttle board, and how to use its main controls.

2
00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:11.389
These Desk lanes show drafts not yet started, work in flight, and results awaiting your review.

3
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.097
To write a task yourself, click the plus on Drafts.

4
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.882
The Stash form asks for a title, optional details, a project and an agent.

5
00:00:23.032 --> 00:00:27.185
One-shot is a single task. Standing repeats on a schedule.

6
00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:30.742
With One-shot selected, Stash saves a draft card.

7
00:00:31.867 --> 00:00:36.112
Or click the star on In flight, and describe an idea in your own words.

8
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:39.396
Pick a project and press Spawn.

9
00:00:39.546 --> 00:00:44.394
An agent turns your words into a task, and its card appears a moment later.

10
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.407
Click any card to open it.

11
00:00:47.557 --> 00:00:52.460
The strip under its title, showing who works it and where, unfolds its actions.

12
00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.209
Write a message for the worker if you like, then choose how to send it.

13
00:00:56.359 --> 00:01:01.059
New session starts a fresh conversation, which reads the task and its notes from the top.

14
00:01:01.209 --> 00:01:05.126
If a worker is still running, the board asks before cutting it off.

15
00:01:05.276 --> 00:01:08.208
Resume requests the task’s previous conversation.

16
00:01:08.358 --> 00:01:11.167
Use it when finished work needs one more change.

17
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:18.705
On a running card, Aloft opens the worker’s conversation, in a terminal, a browser, or a desktop app.

18
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:23.022
When a worker finishes, its outcome waits here for you.

19
00:01:23.172 --> 00:01:28.455
Read it, then press Temper to accept the result, or Discard to set it aside.

20
00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:34.488
To try it, set up Shuttle on one machine, and start with one small task.
